<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33087" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ortygĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ortygĭē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρτυγία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Another name for the isle of Delos</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 3, 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				337</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 183</span></i>
			Müll.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Orty-gĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Ortygian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dea,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Diana</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 694</span></i>
			: boves, <i>of Apollo</i>, bred in Delos, <i><span class="en">id. F. 5,
				692</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An island which forms a part of the city of
			Syracuse</i>, now <i>Siracusa</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3,
				694</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5, 499</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4,
				471</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
